# Project Structure & Git

## File & Folder Conventions

- One component per file. File name must match the component name exactly.
- Co-locate related files in a folder:
  ```
  Button/
    Button.tsx
    Button.test.tsx
    Button.types.ts
    index.ts          ← re-exports Button for clean imports
  ```
- Utility/helper functions go in `/lib` or `/utils`, not inside components.
- Shared types go in `/types` or co-located as `*.types.ts` for domain-specific types.

## Imports

- Order: external libs → internal modules → relative files → styles.
- Use absolute imports (via `tsconfig.json` paths) for anything more than 2 levels deep.

```typescript
// ✅ Clean import order
import { useState } from "react";
import { useQuery } from "@tanstack/react-query";

import { formatDate } from "@/lib/date";
import { UserCard } from "@/components/UserCard";

import { type User } from "./types";
```

## Git Commits (Conventional Commits)

- Format: `type(scope): short description`
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `test`, `docs`, `style`
- Each commit = one logical change. Don't bundle unrelated changes.

```
feat(auth): add JWT refresh token logic
fix(cart): correct quantity calculation on item removal
refactor(api): extract fetchUser into dedicated service file
chore: update dependencies
```
